## CROSS-REPO DEPENDENCIES

- [[paideia-os]] R20b `KIND_IPC_ENDPOINT` (base of
  `sys_cap_transfer`) and R48.M1 `KIND_USER = 0x190`.
- [[paideia-os]] R30-PREP #1631 `KIND_TTY = 0x197` (cf496fb).
- [[paideia-os]] R48b substrate-prep: `KIND_ELEVATE_CHANNEL`,
  `KIND_PDXFS_FILE`, `KIND_PDXFS_TXN`.
- [[paideia-as]] >= v0.33 for `mov_b` narrow-load + `@align`
  attributes on `.bss` slots.
- [[paideia-as]] v0.33-crypto (deferred) for the ML-DSA-65
  sign primitive; libpdx-cap's `SignedInode` publishes the
  layout constants today but wraps no sign call until the
  intrinsic's userspace linkage lands.

## EXAMPLES

    // Example 1 - Refuse a widening cap-forward at exec.
    // shell holds KIND_PDXFS_FILE with RIGHTS_READ; tries to
    // forward RIGHTS_READ|RIGHTS_WRITE to a child. cap_pack_narrowed
    // refuses at the send site with CAP_RIGHTS_WIDENING; the child
    // never receives the widened cap.
    let rc = Cap::cap_pack_narrowed(
        &child_caps[0], 3, KIND_PDXFS_FILE,
        RIGHTS_READ, RIGHTS_READ | RIGHTS_WRITE, dir_endpoint)
    // rc == CAP_RIGHTS_WIDENING (0xFFFFFFF5)

    // Example 2 - Callee refuses an EXTRA cap.
    // ls's caps.decl names KIND_PDXFS_FILE + KIND_TTY.
    // Shell hands KIND_PDXFS_FILE + KIND_TTY + KIND_USER;
    // cap_unpack_checked on the third cap fails EXTRA.
    let rc = Cap::cap_unpack_checked(&received_caps[2])
    // rc == CAP_MANIFEST_EXTRA (0xFFFFFFFB); unpacked_* untouched

    // Example 3 - Render an owner column in `ls --long`.
    KindUserRef::kind_user_ref_reset()
    let rc = KindUserRef::kind_user_ref_decode(&entry_cap)
    if rc == KindUserRef::USER_REF_OK {
        // (Consumer's own syscall path fetches fp0 via
        //  USER_OP_QUERY_FP0 against user_ref_slot.)
        let len = KindUserRef::kind_user_ref_render_hex(fp0)
        // 16 hex bytes now at KindUserRef::user_ref_hex_buf
    }
